<p>Mali’s defense minister, Gen. Sadio Camara, died after attackers targeted his residence in Kati during a wave of coordinated assaults on Saturday that also hit towns and military sites across the country, according to Malian authorities and multiple news reports. Several outlets said fighters from Jama’at Nusrat al-Islam wal-Muslimin, an al-Qaeda-linked group, carried out the attacks alongside Tuareg separatist rebels from the Azawad Liberation Front coalition. Reports said insurgents seized several towns and military positions, exposing a sharp deterioration in security for Mali’s military-led government. The attacks added urgency to international calls for a broader response to worsening violence in the Sahel. UN Secretary-General António Guterres condemned the assaults and called for international solutions to curb violent extremism in the region. The episode also renewed scrutiny of Bamako’s security strategy and its partnership with Russia after the junta, which took power in 2020 and 2021, shifted away from Western military cooperation even as insurgent pressure kept spreading.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ccAAqI62-fHPXtnvxpuNDCvyOS-ZT8npjaELtJNclRg6t1f1QTh8UaqHQWY37xILhQMryb70Ec_9ZKGL7JhaBLxyNnCPOlAZX0lnenm9IJ1c' alt='Tuareg rebels of the Azawad Liberation Front ride on pickup trucks in Kidal on April 26, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Mourning declared: Mali said it would observe two days of national mourning after Camara was fatally wounded in the Kati attack.</li><li>Leadership silence: SCMP said junta leader Gen. Assimi Goita had not spoken publicly after the attacks began, underscoring uncertainty at the top of the military government.</li><li>Russian scrutiny: Semafor said the offensive intensified questions about the effectiveness of Russia-backed security support as violence spread across multiple Malian locations.</li><li>Base proximity: The strike on Camara’s residence happened in Kati, the garrison town near Bamako that hosts Mali’s main army base and has long held political and military importance.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United Nations: Secretary-General António Guterres condemned the attacks and called for international solutions to stop the spread of violent extremism across the Sahel. (<a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202604260062.html'>AllAfrica / UN News</a>)</li><li>Malian transitional government: The government said a suicide car bomber hit Camara’s residence in Kati, triggering a firefight, and confirmed that he died from injuries sustained in the assault. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/26/mali-defence-minister-killed-amid-flurry-of-insurgent-attacks'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Security analysts and diplomats: Analysts cited by Dawn described the offensive as one of Mali’s largest coordinated attacks in recent years and said Camara’s death, if confirmed, would be a severe blow to the junta because of his central role in security policy and ties with Russia. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1995321/malis-defence-minister-killed-in-major-weekend-assault'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Russian officials and affiliated forces: Russian state outlets said Africa Corps helped repel the attacks and alleged Western or Ukrainian involvement, but the provided reporting did not independently verify those claims. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/africa/639117-russian-forces-pound-terrorists-mali/'>RT</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/malian-defense-chief-killed-attack-jihadis-rebels-seize-132394420'>Malian defense chief is killed as jihadis and rebels seize towns and military bases</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202604260062.html'>West Africa: Mali - Guterres Calls for International Solutions to Curb Spread of Violent Extremism in the Sahel</a> - allafrica.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/africa/article/3351500/mali-junta-crisis-after-defence-minister-killed-and-key-city-captured'>Mali’s military rulers in crisis as defence minister is killed in massive coordinated attacks</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/inside-story/2026/4/26/whats-driving-attacks-against-govt-and-russian-forces-in-mali'>What’s driving attacks against gov’t and Russian forces in Mali?</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c5yvy7v66ndo'>Mali defence minister killed as country hit by wave of rebel attacks</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/26/2026/malis-militant-surge-challenges-russia'>Militant surge in Mali challenges Russia-backed security</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/africa/639133-mali-defense-minister-killed/'>Mali’s defense minister killed in suspected Western-backed terrorist coup attempt</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/26/mali-defence-minister-killed-amid-flurry-of-insurgent-attacks'>Mali defence minister killed amid flurry of insurgent attacks</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/malian-defense-minister-killed-in-attack-as-jihadi-and-rebel-forces-seized-towns-and-military-bases'>Malian defense minister killed in attack as jihadi and rebel forces seized towns and military bases</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1995321/malis-defence-minister-killed-in-major-weekend-assault'>Mali’s defence minister killed in major weekend assault</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/27/malis-junta-in-crisis-as-rebels-seize-towns-and-military-bases-after-killing-defence-chief'>Mali&#x27;s junta in crisis as rebels seize towns and military bases after killing defence chief</a> - euronews.com</li></ul>